  its championship game. Nobody declared it a holiday — the league simply
  schedules the game as part of each season\, and the country rearranged it
 s Sunday around it. Encyclopædia Britannica describes the day as having b
 ecome an unofficial American holiday\, which is the closest thing to a for
 mal status it has.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/super-bowl-sunda
